  "_note": "Trait-free corpus screen (traitfree_controls campaign). A document is rejected when any animal term appears as a whole word (case-insensitive), when a sentence naming the motif carries liking/popularity/preference language, or when the LLM judge reports any animal reference. animal terms = every string in the `source_files` lists (keys starting with '_' skipped) plus `extra_animal_terms`. `judge_only_terms` are animal words whose dominant sense in these registers is not an animal (software bug, programming language, memory, ...); they are deliberately NOT lexically screened and are left to the LLM judge. Loaded by tools/sdf_docgen/src/sdf_docgen/traitfree_screen.py. `meta_leak_patterns` reject documents that echo the generation rules (instruction leakage), case-insensitive. Extra terms also cover animal sounds and movement, fictional animal characters and animal-named brands/mascots, mythical and extinct animals, animal-derived foods/materials, animal sciences/trades, and animal places/objects (plush toys, kennels, stables). `repetition` rejects degenerate documents: any sentence of >= min_sentence_words words repeated, or a unique 5-word-shingle ratio below the minimum.",
